questions.q:
Consider the function:
int f(int n){ if(n<=1) return 1; return f(n-1)+f(n-2); }
What is the value of f(6)?

What is the final list after this code runs on the list 1->2->3->4->5?
p = head;
while(p != NULL && p->next != NULL){ t = p->data; p->data = p->next->data; p->next->data = t; p = p->next->next; }

Consider:
int p(int x,int n){ if(n==0) return 1; int t=p(x,n/2); if(n%2==0) return t*t; return x*t*t; }
How many calls to p are made, including the first, for p(3,16)?

The list 1->2->3->4 is reversed with this loop:
prev=NULL; cur=head;
while(cur){ nxt=cur->next; cur->next=prev; prev=cur; cur=nxt; }
After exactly two iterations, what chain does prev point to?
